  lines:
  - "\u201CNeed some company?\u201D"
  - "\u201CNeed some company?\u201D"
  - 'Spike lit up a bit, smirking from ear to ear.

'
  - 'Spike lit up a bit, smirking from ear to ear.

'
  - "\u201CWell of course\u201D\r\n"
  - "\u201CWell of course\u201D\r\n"
  - "He lets out a teasing smile to Claire before the both of us begin walking to
    Professor Draco\u2019s office.\r\n"
  - "He lets out a teasing smile to Claire before the both of us begin walking to
    Professor Draco\u2019s office.\r\n"
  - "\u201CWhat brought you here with me?\u201D"
  - "\u201CWhat brought you here with me?\u201D"
  - Spike asks half expectant of an answer to boost his ego.
  - Spike asks half expectant of an answer to boost his ego.
  - "\u201CHonestly speaking , I wanted to see the Professor\u2019s office first
    hand\u201D"
  - "\u201CHonestly speaking , I wanted to see the Professor\u2019s office first
    hand\u201D"
  - "\u201CHonestly speaking , I wanted to see the Professor\u2019s office first
    hand\u201D"
  - Spike just laugh as he clicks his tongue
  - Spike just laugh as he clicks his tongue
  - "\u201CWeird girl\u201D\r\n"
  - "\u201CWeird girl\u201D\r\n"
  - We approach his doors. I pause expecting Spike to knock and announce our arrival,
    he instead flings both doors open as if it were the entrance of his home.
  - We approach his doors. I pause expecting Spike to knock and announce our arrival,
    he instead flings both doors open as if it were the entrance of his home.
  - "\u201CWell would you look at that, the old bastard\u2019s running\u201D\r\n"
  - "\u201CWell would you look at that, the old bastard\u2019s running\u201D\r\n"
  - Spike exclaims half annoyed, I just take a second to indulge the scenery.
  - Spike exclaims half annoyed, I just take a second to indulge the scenery.
  - His office was no more- so a huge study. With bookshelves from floor to ceiling
    and a large dark oak desk with two couches displayed in front. It was dimly lit
    , lit by secondary light options instead of one overhead bulb with candles perched
    around like trinkets, lit
  - His office was no more- so a huge study. With bookshelves from floor to ceiling
    and a large dark oak desk with two couches displayed in front. It was dimly lit
    , lit by secondary light options instead of one overhead bulb with candles perched
    around like trinkets, lit
  - "That had to be a safety hazard. The carpet was blood red with a mini fireplace
    just behind the desk. Spike nonchalantly takes a seat kicking his feet up as
    he waits. Phone in hand, eyes to screen. \r\n"
  - "That had to be a safety hazard. The carpet was blood red with a mini fireplace
    just behind the desk. Spike nonchalantly takes a seat kicking his feet up as
    he waits. Phone in hand, eyes to screen. \r\n"
  - 'But how could he possibly not feel what I''m feeling right now. '
  - 'But how could he possibly not feel what I''m feeling right now. '
  - "As if we\u2019re not the only beings in this room, I swear if it was quiet enough
    I would hear the books whisper to one another.\r\n"
  - "As if we\u2019re not the only beings in this room, I swear if it was quiet enough
    I would hear the books whisper to one another.\r\n"
  - "\u201COi stop wandering about curly and take a seat, he\u2019s fussy about what
    we touch in here\u201D"
  - "\u201COi stop wandering about curly and take a seat, he\u2019s fussy about what
    we touch in here\u201D"
  - 'I abide Spike and take a seat, awarding a full view of his desk. My eyes scan
    it carefully. '
  - 'I abide Spike and take a seat, awarding a full view of his desk. My eyes scan
    it carefully. '
  - "So far there\u2019s only been proof that the school  pays him well, nothing
    really screaming of Occult. \r\n"
  - "So far there\u2019s only been proof that the school  pays him well, nothing
    really screaming of Occult. \r\n"
  - "His desk is crowded with piles of books and miscellaneous paper to stationery,
    in the corner sits a skull which I presume to be fake and a few classic literature
    books such as Lolita, a controversial read definitely. \r\n"
  - "His desk is crowded with piles of books and miscellaneous paper to stationery,
    in the corner sits a skull which I presume to be fake and a few classic literature
    books such as Lolita, a controversial read definitely. \r\n"
  - 'My eyes land on a paper and a pen spilling ink onto it, placed atop the pile
    of books as it was written on in a rush, I look carefully without making obvious
    my line of sight.

'
  - 'My eyes land on a paper and a pen spilling ink onto it, placed atop the pile
    of books as it was written on in a rush, I look carefully without making obvious
    my line of sight.

'
  - "Bull\u2026Prison "
  - "Bull\u2026Prison "
  - Followed by a contact and time set of 08:00-17:00 and 09:00-16:00.
  - Followed by a contact and time set of 08:00-17:00 and 09:00-16:00.
  - ' I take a mental note immediately, fishing out my own phone to write it down
    just as I begin typing the stack of books slide off his desk as papers fly around
    the room, Spike immediately glares at me to which I throw my hands in the air.

'
  - ' I take a mental note immediately, fishing out my own phone to write it down
    just as I begin typing the stack of books slide off his desk as papers fly around
    the room, Spike immediately glares at me to which I throw my hands in the air.

'
  - "\u201CI didn't touch anything\u201D\r\n"
  - "\u201CI didn't touch anything\u201D\r\n"
  - "I answer defensively, he sighs and gets up from his couch to try and help. \r\n"
  - "I answer defensively, he sighs and gets up from his couch to try and help. \r\n"
  - "\u201CNo don't fret I've got it \u201D"
  - "\u201CNo don't fret I've got it \u201D"
  - I assure him , he shrugs and goes back on his phone. I don't need him to see
    the snooping I'm about to do, this was a sign from God.
  - I assure him , he shrugs and goes back on his phone. I don't need him to see
    the snooping I'm about to do, this was a sign from God.
  - "I get to my knees and hunch over, sorting page to page that fell down, it ranged
    from flyers he was probably handed without wanting them to invoices and receipts,
    before I could pocket a receipt for later , A grey corner sticking out a book
    caught my eye, a newspaper article tucked away. \r\n"
  - "I get to my knees and hunch over, sorting page to page that fell down, it ranged
    from flyers he was probably handed without wanting them to invoices and receipts,
    before I could pocket a receipt for later , A grey corner sticking out a book
    caught my eye, a newspaper article tucked away. \r\n"
  - "I immediately grab it , looking to Spike\u2019s direction to see if he caught
    me, his eyes were still on his screen, I sigh relieved , I look to it\u2019s
    title to see if it held any value and once I red the title I immediately folded
    it up and slid it into my satchel but as soon as my hands hit the carpet to clear
    up the mess, a dark shadow loomed over me. "
  - "I immediately grab it , looking to Spike\u2019s direction to see if he caught
    me, his eyes were still on his screen, I sigh relieved , I look to it\u2019s
    title to see if it held any value and once I red the title I immediately folded
    it up and slid it into my satchel but as soon as my hands hit the carpet to clear
    up the mess, a dark shadow loomed over me. "
  - "\u201CAnd what exactly is going on here?\u201D\r\n"
  - "\u201CAnd what exactly is going on here?\u201D\r\n"
  - "Professor Draco\u2019s voice is a lot more authoritative than usual, I nervously
    get to my feet."
  - "Professor Draco\u2019s voice is a lot more authoritative than usual, I nervously
    get to my feet."
  - "\u201CH-hello sir I was just accompanying Spike, then your books just fell off
    your desk and I tried gathering them-\u201D"
  - "\u201CH-hello sir I was just accompanying Spike, then your books just fell off
    your desk and I tried gathering them-\u201D"
  - "\u201CI think it\u2019s better you be on your way, Nyx\u201D\r\n"
  - "\u201CI think it\u2019s better you be on your way, Nyx\u201D\r\n"
  - He says as my eyes widen and I nod, I immediately stand up and look at his desk
    one last time , that's when I see it.
  - He says as my eyes widen and I nod, I immediately stand up and look at his desk
    one last time , that's when I see it.
  - My pop quiz sheet from earlier separated from the bigger pile, as distinct from
    the dried up blood mark, my heart dropped further with a closer look.
  - My pop quiz sheet from earlier separated from the bigger pile, as distinct from
    the dried up blood mark, my heart dropped further with a closer look.
  - My quiz was different.
  - My quiz was different.
  - It was all on One topic.
  - It was all on One topic.
  - Dream Psychology.
  - Dream Psychology.
  - 'I immediately clutch my bag and hastily walk out the office and once the doors
    are closed and I''ve walked a good distance away I bolt down the corridor and
    straight into the female bathrooms. '
  - 'I immediately clutch my bag and hastily walk out the office and once the doors
    are closed and I''ve walked a good distance away I bolt down the corridor and
    straight into the female bathrooms. '
